            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Military Reforms</strong><br>\nUnderstanding the empire's military needs, Theodosius restructured the Roman army. He incorporated barbarian units into the army's ranks, which both alleviated manpower shortages and integrated the various peoples within the empire. These reforms helped to stabilize the Eastern frontier and were crucial for the subsequent military campaigns.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Administrative Reorganization</strong><br>\nTheodosius also undertook administrative reforms. He realized that a well-organized bureaucracy was essential for the management of empire affairs. His reorganization efforts improved the efficiency of the government, helping it to manage internal affairs more effectively and maintain its territories.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Battle of the Goths</strong><br>\nIn 394 AD, Theodosius fought against the Goths in the Battle of the Frigidus. This conflict was significant as it helped to secure the unity of the empire. His victory over the Goths solidified his control and weakened the autonomy of barbarian tribes within the empire's borders.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
